 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? It means the bike isn't fitting you properly. It should feel comfortable when sit on it, and the gears should shift smoothly. That's a common sign. The seat might be too low, or the stem too short. That's usually the handlebars being too high. Try lowering them bit, or swapping stem for longer one. Not always. Local bike shop can often do it for free. First try some simple adjustments yourself, then ask them. A good shop will do a test ride for you too.",
